I did finally resolve this. After making about 5 calls to HP/Compaq
support phone lines, I finally managed to speak to someone who knew
that Tru64 was a product they sell. Just about everyone else looked it
up on their computers and could find no record of any such product.
Even the guy I spoke to at their password centre had never heard of
Tru64! 

Anyway, the guy I finally spoke to suggested I ran 'lmf register'.
That allowed me to enter the details with a text editor, which solved
it. The system is now up and running okay. The graphics is not set up
properly (running 640x480), but networked to my Sun Ultra 80, I have a
decent display of CDE on that. So all seems fine. 

I will join the Tru64 managers mailing list (anyone know how ??) and
no doubt will be flooding that with really basic questions soon. 

I must say, for $100 one gets quite a bit, including a set of
development tools, which I assume generate faster code for the Alpha
than what gcc does. 


