On Tue, May 06, 2003 at 03:07:04PM -0400, Peter Petrakis wrote:
> I wonder what those numbers would look like compiled with ccc and linked
> with libcpml? I had some ccc compiled ssl rpms around here somewhere.

'libcpml' is likely irrelevant here as these will be integer
calculations only (a lot of bit banging). 'ccc' could be interesting;
especially if tuned for a processor optimizations were used.  You may
gain on an instruction scheduling or at least there is a hope.

Keep also in mind that the last time I looked this code quite obviously
assumed 32-bit registers and used some tricks to benefit from that fact.
Not a bad assumption in general as a vast majority of processers on
which this will be used will be 32-bits; at least for a while yet.
Touching it is a quite delicate operation as it has to be first
correct and a speed is a distant secondary as long as this is fast
enough.  In practice the later is usually the case. :-)

  Michal




