It appears that my console flash ROM has become corrupted and SRM will not
load, in fact I have not output to the monitor, but I got error messages on
the control unit.

"P0 fail 3 from 0"
> "P0 fail 6 from 0"
> then after a pause,
> "P0 fail 36 from 0"

The messages mean there are 2 or 3 failures in the start-up of the flash ROM
but the CPUs light up and the service manual says that means they are
functioning correctly.

I have put the fail safe loader floppy into the drive and it started up with
the error messages followed by "FSL V5.0 on CPU 0".

There is no output to the monitor and I want to complete the procedure by
using the LFU command to update (re-install) the SRM console firmware.

I am trying to connect using a serial cable and HyperTerminal from a WN2K
box but it is not recording any output.

This should not be occurring according to the manual because output should
go to com 1 during start-up, so I suspect I have not set it up right.

I have set up the HyperTerminal connection as terminal emulation as VT-100,
baud rate 9600, flow control as none, 8,1, none.

Has anyone on the list got any suggestions how to connect on the serial
line?

Is there a key combination I can use to send output to the monitor?

Any help appreciated.

Simon



