>
>     This is "No Longer Available" through traditional channels.  If the
>customer wants it, they have to download it via the Internet.  I strongly
>urge against running this release of Red Hat Linux.

That is their perogative I guess, as it is their product to 
market/sell/distribute/support.

>     There is no support available through Red Hat for this product.

And there never was any support from Red Hat for Red Hat Linux 
7.2 for Alpha.  It was an Alpha port done under contract for 
Compaq/HP.  HP provide(s|d) all support as it is their product.  
This is why it is also only available for download/purchase from 
HP.


>     As of 12-31-03, Red Hat will no longer be providing updates for this
>release.

That information has false inference.  Red Hat has never provided
updates for Red Hat Linux 7.2 for Alpha ever.  As I mention 
above, it was contracted for HP, with no support or updates from 
Red Hat.  HP has put some updates on their ftp site over time, 
but they were produced by HP, not by Red Hat.

Other than creating the original 7.2/Alpha distribution, Red Hat 
hasn't had anything to do with it since.

That said, it'd be nice to see a port of Red Hat Linux 9 to 
Alpha.  ;o)


