With regards to your message at 06:49 AM 5/23/03, Mike Foley. Where you stated:

>    So, just another case of Maurice jumping the gun
>    and injecting a bit of drama into the remaining Alpha customers
>    lives?
>
>                                                       mike


A case of reporting what the official voices tell me, and by doing so 
priming them to fix their rather convoluted methods of doing business, Mike.

All I tried to do is order a bunch of copies of Red Hat boxed sets, as I 
have done many times before.

And as is often the case I was frustrated by being thrown obstacles in 
doing this.
If I had not "jumped the gun" there would have been no resolution, and at 
least 25 more people would not have had the chance to run Linux on their 
new ( and old) Alphas.

While it is possible to buy RH 7.2 for Alpha online IF you are located in 
the USA, it is NOT possible for people to do this outside of the USA.

As the HP website points out:
"HP part number: QA-6M1AA-H8
Call 1-800-448-6737 (U.S. only)
Available outside the U.S. from HP's resellers and distributors. "

And we are one of about 2 remaining resellers for this application.

The other wrinkle in all of this that bears pointing out is that if one 
were to want the excellent compilers and libs one used to be able to buy 
7.1, which included these.
With 7.2 they are not included, and unless one is an "enthusiast" you would 
need to buy these, at a pretty hefty price tag for licensing.
While 7.1 is rather old, at least it includes the licenses, and it is then 
trivial to upgrade to 7.2 and retain the right to use these legally..

Hopefully that will help with your understanding of this, Mike.

Ta!


With our best regards,

