Hello list, William,

Thursday, May 22, 2003, 6:06:58 PM, you wrote:

WHM> Interestingly, Red Hat may be dead, but SuSE has managed to "bootleg" a 
WHM> new version for Alpha.

Sorry to inform you, but you missed the point!
SuSE AXP is dead too :



Fri May  9 14:35:14 MEST 2003

Dear SuSE Linux for Alpha/AXP,

SuSE Linux 7.1-axp has been discontinued. You can still find it in
the /pub/suse/discontinued/axp/ tree.

The 7.1 was the last distribution that was available for Alpha.
Please have a look at the /pub/suse/axp/supplementary/ tree in a few
days from now. There will be a newer distribution, but it won't have any
security (and other) updates from SuSE. As such, it might be useful,
but we regret that there is currently not more that we can do.

Regards,
Roman Drahtmüller.

Roman Drahtmüller,
Christopher Mahmood,
<ftpadmin@suse.com>.
 

(source: ftp.suse.com/pub/suse/axp)



Slowly we're runing out of optins :(


Regards, Zsolt

