With regards to your message at 05:20 PM 5/24/03, Uncle George. Where you 
stated:
>did you not write this
>"Have a beef - contribute!"
>
>Its also somewhat counter productive to the continual support of the alpha 
>line, if all you have to suggest is to go use another 64bit machine 
>architecture.


George, the whole point of this discussion is 64 bit OS and 64 bit platforms.

Are you planning to buy a new Alpha system some time soon?
I doubt it.

OTOH, there is a very good viable platform now in Opteron, at a very 
reasonable price.

The way this is going it will soon sound like some Atari ST or Amiga users 
list.

While we are on this list to provide support and a bit for nostalgia sake, 
the fact is "it's over" as far as Alpha is concerned.

Michal's comment was to point out that at least on Opteron Linux systems 
Open Office runs quite nicely, without any extra effort needed by us or you.

I am not happy that Alpha is in demise either, but there is little I can do 
about it.
And, quite frankly, I am happy that Opteron is out, with good performance, 
at a decent price point.

I can recall back on this list a few years ago all the wistful dreaming by 
people predicting/dreaming about the "next Alpha board" that would be fast 
and cheap, and with good industry support.

We have that 6 bit platform now, so my recommendation is to use it.

If it makes you happier, put an Alpha sticker on the outside of the box..




With our best regards,

