On Sat, 24 May 2003, Uncle George wrote:

>I think that you will find that OpenOffice is missing from the Alpha 
>distribution. I suppose that there is a reason for this, but i dont 
>think that the logical reason is that the source is 64bit clean.

You don't seem to be aware of how RPM packages are built and 
maintained.

The spec file, is _inside_ the src.rpm of *every* package.  You
obtain the spec file, by downloading the source code rpm
(src.rpm) of the package you want to
develop/debug/improve/fix/port/whatever, then install it.

>Wether or not you have a 64bit clean src .rpm, there is no distributed 
>binary rpm spec file.

RPM spec files are _not_ binary files.  They are human editable 
text files.  And as I said above, they are a part of the src.rpm.

>This makes it somewhat hard to fill ( contribute ) in the gaps
>left out by the compaq/redhat relationship.

There is nothing hard about downloading and installing a src.rpm
to obtain the spec file, which is useless without the rest of the
src.rpm, and the src.rpm is useless without the spec file, which 
is why it is contained inside the src.rpm.

You may want to read Maximum RPM, or the RPM HOWTO before 
proceeding.


-- 
Mike A. Harris     ftp://people.redhat.com/mharris
OS Systems Engineer - XFree86 maintainer - Red Hat



