We have been working on 4.3 at HP.  Mike is correct, there are lots of 
dependencies and it has required lots of work.  We are in process of testing 
2.4.18-27 for RH-7.2.  The 2.4.18-27 kernel has been updated for 4.3 
including the DRI bits.  We still have a couple of issues that we need to 
correct before this kernel is ready for commercial use. These bits are 
available for testing from:

	 ftp://alpha.crl.dec.com/pub/linux/people/france/kernel-2.4.18

As these bits are still in the testing phase, they should be used at your own 
risk.  Please remember that the post install process does not update 
/etc/about.conf and that you will need to edit this file by hand before 
rebooting your system.

Currently after significant patching we do have 4.3 working on a handful of 
systems.   With the time and resources available, it will probably be minimum 
of 30 to 60 days before we have something stable enough to release.

Best Regards,


--George



