>I guess i dont understand. exactly what set of rpm instructions was use 
>to create, for example, this bin file 
>"foomatic-1.1-0.20011218.3.5.alpha.rpm"

The command used to create that binary alpha RPM was:

    bhc -ns dist-7.2-alpha foomatic-1.1-0.20011218.3.5.src.rpm

I suspect you're not looking for the command that was used to 
create that binary rpm, but rather the command that _you_ can use 
to create that rpm.  In that case it would be:

    rpmbuild --rebuild foomatic-1.1-0.20011218.3.5.src.rpm

Again, RTFMing the RPM-HOWTO, and Maximum RPM would provide you 
with these and many more answers.

