On Sun, 25 May 2003, Ivan Kokshaysky wrote:

>> There hasn't been any widescale testing of 4.3.0 on Alpha that 
>> I'm aware of, so it may not be too stable.  THen again, it might 
>> be more stable.  Hard to say.
>
>I had couple of problems with 4.3.0:
>- Detection of the primary adapter is broken. You have to
>  set explicit PCI id in XF86Config to get the card detected
>  as *secondary*. However, switching to VGA text console won't work then
>  (most drivers don't save/restore VGA state for secondary adapters).
>- Rather old bug in mga driver (since 4.1.0, IIRC) - the driver
>  attempts to read the video ROM *before* enabling it. Naturally,
>  this causes annoying machine check on certain platforms.
>
>Fixes appended. Mike, could you include these in XFree rpms / push
>it upstream?

I don't personally submit patches upstream that I can't verify 
personally, or to which I don't have time to verify personally, 
as XFree86.org gets pissy on the submitter if they haven't tested 
a patch they've submitted, however...

To submit a patch upstream, submit a bug report to XFree86.org
via http://bugs.xfree86.org indicating the above info, and attach
the patch to the bug report via bugzilla file attachment.

If you'd like me to include the patch in Red Hat rpm packaging
also, please submit an RFE in Red Hat bugzilla with the patch
attached also (or just a http link to XFree86 bugzilla) and I'd
be glad to review it and probably include it in our rpms if it 
checks out ok with other Alpha folk (George France, Jeff, 
etc.) too. 



