picking up an Athlon 64 once it is released, you can run the
GinGin64 technology preview from the above URL on it for the time
being, as well as the standard 32bit x86 releases of Red Hat
Linux.

I'm not sure if this answers your question exactly or not, but it
is all of the information which I can provide.  If anyone
requires more specific information, please call Red Hat sales at
1-888-RED-HAT1 as they may or may not be able to provide
additional information.

Also, keep an eye out for Red Hat press releases, by monitoring
our press release page on our website occasionally.  Whenever we
do announce current or future products publically, we generally
make press releases about them.

You may also wish to join amd64-list@redhat.com to stay in tune 
with Red Hat products on AMD64.

Hope this helps.


