Er, when I said, "full," and mean "full development cycle."  Sorry I did
not clarify that.

But yes, the Pentium 4 _is_ a "new design" and not an incremental
redesign of the Pentium Pro like the Pentium II and III were.  I do
concur and apologize for not being clear in that regard

> The Pentium 4 took a lot longer than 18 months
