Of which I do not doubt is true.

But it is clear to me that many aspects of the design of the Pentium 4
were left rather "unfinished."  At least that's exactly the term one
former Intel engineer I worked with put it.  [ He had a general distain
for the entire vector/SIMD "marketing focus" of the Pentium 4. ]

