What really is the point of this thread? You had a fantastic technology
that over many years was chipped away at because it wasn't mainstream (ergo
cheap). The common wisdom (and I uset he term loosely) drove everyone to
belive that if it were more Intel'ish all our problems would be solved.

So now we have Intel repackaging Alpha as Itanium2, which has a lot of
steam behind it, and I'll admit the prices have yet to come down, but you
have a proven technology, with operating systems and ISV's developers who's
put thier money where thier mouths are..and we can somehow only find new
ways to poke holes....

It's so easy to jump in behind the newest..latest greatest that looks like
a super deal...But let's go back to what our parents tought us. You buy
something cheap and that's what you get.

It's easy to be the armchair QB.....Invest...write the OS, write the
compilers and the debuggers, write the libraries, write the layered
applications that link everything needed within even a simple environment,
and then try to go out and kill another technology. 

It's called transition or migration. Get over it. Threads like this over
the years have done nothing more than encourage the sale of Alpha
technology to Intel. You wanted Intel, now you've got Intel. Move on, or at
the very least, let's close this sort of bashing.

btw...how much does AMD receive each year from Intel so they don't have to
worry about FTC issues. It's burried, but I'll bet if a person were to
write a few lines of decent code, he/she could find it. When ya do, let the
rest of us know what the exact number is....please.

~m


