Benton, Marco wrote:

>64bit NT/Alpha????  when?  where?  do you mean 64bit VLM?  NT 4 was never 64
>bit native.  i dont even think NT 5.0 (as it was called back then) was 64bit
>clean.  but i could be wrong...  but then again, i remember the 1st
>iterations of Linux/Alpha were not 64-bit either.
>

    There was a version of NT-64 (NT 5.0 in 64-bit mode) running in the
    labs of Microsoft and DECwest for a LONG time. When Compaq bought
    DEC, the PC Expo of that summer had the DEC folks living in the Compaq
    booth. Next to my demo was a 64-bit NT running a 64-bit SQL Server 
in VLM
    mode. Mont Francisco was running it. That was 1998.

    Windows 2000 for Alpha also had FX!32 checked in to the source pool. It
    ran in kernel mode and was much cleaner than the user mode FX!32. It 
just
    worked.

    64-bit NT ran in the Microsoft labs long after DEC/Compaq punted NT on
    Alpha. They needed something to continue development on, after all, then
    only had Merced simulators at that time! It's my understanding those 
systems
    are long gone.

    There were alot of shoulda-woulda-coulda's around then.

                                                                         
