Uncle George wrote:
> I guess i dont understand. exactly what set of rpm instructions was use 
> to create, for example, this bin file 
> "foomatic-1.1-0.20011218.3.5.alpha.rpm"

I answered this off-list for you. Well, not foomatic, specifically, I 
used cvsd.

The spec file that you find in source-rpm packages have instructions on 
how/where to get the source tarballs, the patches, how to apply same, 
how to build the binary-rpm package, and the instructions to run while 
installing the rpm.

You can also ask for the install-scripts that are to be run from an 
rpm-binary file, without having access to the source-rpm. (rpm -q -p 
rpmbinaryfile.rpm --scripts).

It sounds like there are several aspects to rpm that you'd like 
answered, besides what I discussed. While I await questions, you are 
aware of www.rpm.org and the book 'Maximum RPM' (whose source is found 
at rpm.org)?




