As it says with the t&C of Debian - this software comes with absolutely no
waranty use at your own risk.....

Basically what they are saying is that this is free software developed by
people for nothing for their own reasons. These people are not out to make
money out of these particular efforts. Of course we all need money to live
on to buy food, clothing etc...

Why then do big companies use this software - I'll tell you because it's
cheap - free even - and big companies and any company if they have any sense
have only one purpose - to make $Money$ not to make the world a fine and
dandy place by spreading the gospel of GNU software.

The reason Alpha was killed off - well maybe plus a bit of politics - was
that other platforms have the potential to make more money or so the people
who made such decisions thought.

No one in business really cares about Linux they just use it because it's
cheap and there are people out there with the right experience who are ready
to sell the skills for a relatively inexpensive rate.

Where that leaves everyone is anyone's guess but it might be wise to look
back in history to a person called Phil Katz who realeased some free
software which everyone on this list has used at some point and what
happened to him.... take a look on google....

It's just wise to remember it's tough out there and really the bottom line
comes first....

cheers,






