For ALPHA:
you will need at least 700mb for the source.

if you do get it to compile ( i did not say work ), it will grow to more 
than 2.5gb ( yes giga bytes ).

then there are the issue regarding compilers & mozilla. current OO 
source(s) would like u to use gcc version 3 and above. if you cant use 
ver 3 then they suggest ver 2.95.  It does not appear that the OO folks 
are  going back to gcc 2, but there are ( legacy ) scripts that are 
suppose to work with gcc 2.95.  

If u stick with gcc ver 2, then the mozilla-devel on alpha is just fine. 
If you go with gcc 3, well then u need to rebuild mozilla with gcc 3 ( 
you'l also find that mozilla does not compile for gcc 3. There are 
issues the name mangling differences in g++ 3 & asm )

You'll also need to be aware of something called dwarf2 for g++3 ( maybe 
even g++ 2 ).
/gat

