> you'l also find that mozilla does not compile for gcc 3. There are 
> issues the name mangling differences in g++ 3 & asm )
 
SuSE Linux 8.1 Alpha Edition contains a mozilla package that was
compiled with gcc 3.2. We also have mozilla compiling with gcc 3.3.
If you want to look at the patches, check the src rpm for SuSE's ftp
server or drop me a note, I can send them to you.
Mozilla is a piece of **** in that regard, as every platform has
differences in the mangling and the calling sequence. So no mozilla on a
platform where you don't want to hack assembler. (For IA64 there's only
a generic port to libffi available)

OpenOffice does not even get close to compiling here, as the scripts
they use to set everything up are a huge mess and fail for lots of
reasons that are not the usual suspects when porting code to 64bit
platforms.

  Stefan

